# {{ app_title }}

{{ project_description }}

A local macOS desktop app: Python with [pywebview](https://pywebview.flowrl.com/) for the window,
and a web UI styled with [Tailwind](https://tailwindcss.com/) and
[DaisyUI](https://daisyui.com/), using [Alpine.js](https://alpinejs.dev/) for UI state.

## Setup

- Install [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)
- From the root directory run `uv sync`

## Running

```bash
make run   # open the app
make dev   # open it with the web inspector (right-click → Inspect)
```

## Settings

Set these as environment variables, or in a `.env` file in the repo root:

| Variable | Default | What it does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `{{ env_prefix }}_DATA_DIR` | `data/` | Where the app keeps its files: `prefs.json`{% if include_database %} and `{{ project_name }}.db`{% endif %}. |
| `{{ env_prefix }}_DEBUG` | off | `1` turns on the web inspector. `make dev` sets it. |

## Development

```bash
make format  # ruff and djlint
make lint    # ruff, ty and djlint
make test    # pytest
make check   # all three
```

## Stack

Frontend libraries are vendored in `src/{{ project_name }}/web/vendor/`, so the app needs no build
step and no network:

